          "atMs": 21400
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "image": "videos/05-brain-washes-itself/3.jpg",
      "seconds": 23.86,
      "text": "Think of a city that can only run its street cleaners after the traffic stops. The brain cannot think and deep clean at the same time, so it schedules the second shift for the night. Among the waste it clears is amyloid beta, the protein that accumulates in Alzheimer's disease. Which reframes a short night. Not lost hours. A skipped shift.",
      "delivery": {
        "rate": 8,
        "pitch": -1
      },
      "clips": [
        {
